 "comments": [
  {
   "address": 25600,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Twenty consecutive 64-byte sprite slots in VIC bank $4000. Each slot begins with 21 rows of three pixel bytes, and the last byte is outside the displayed height."
  },
  {
   "address": 26624,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Four sprite slots after the first sixteen mission frames. The VIC slot positions relative to bank $4000 are $A0-$A3."
  },
  {
   "address": 49152,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Four rows of four character codes per 16-byte tile. The map renderer resolves a tile ID through the resident screen-code pointer tables, then indexes this pattern with the character coordinates modulo four."
  },
  {
   "address": 50176,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The stage maps can reference tile ID $44 here. Four character rows at $C440 form its 16-byte shape."
  },
  {
   "address": 52992,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Tile-indexed colour bytes. The initial playfield renderer at $17CD reads these in parallel with the tile character pointers and $1882 writes the chosen value to colour RAM."
  },
  {
   "address": 53248,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Primary 256-character graphics source. The resident wipe routine at $1DC2 enables RAM under I/O and copies the selected pixel rows to the live character set at $4000."
  },
  {
   "address": 54272,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Rows for character codes $80-$FF in the main stage's 256-glyph set. The masked copy selects them through the same eight-byte stride as the lower codes."
  },
  {
   "address": 55296,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Alternate 256-character graphics source in RAM below the I/O window. The resident wipe routine chooses this source when $1902 is set, unless the alternate scene flag $ADF7 takes priority."
  },
  {
   "address": 56320,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The upper half of the alternate stage's eight-byte character slots, read under CIA and expansion register addresses with I/O banked out."
  },
  {
   "address": 57344,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage 1 grid, 64 entries per row and first 9 rows. Each byte selects one 4 \u00d7 4 character tile through the split table at $08D6/$09C6."
  },
  {
   "address": 57920,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage 1 grid, 64 entries per row and first 9 rows. The engine uses the low three bits for world-coordinate attribute lookups and modifies the grid during play."
  },
  {
   "address": 58496,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage 2 grid, 32 entries per row and first 31 rows. Each byte selects one 4 \u00d7 4 character tile through the split table at $08D6/$09C6."
  },
  {
   "address": 59680,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage 2 grid, 32 entries per row and first 31 rows. The engine uses the low three bits for world-coordinate attribute lookups and modifies the grid during play."
  },
  {
   "address": 60864,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage 3 grid, 68 entries per row and first 9 rows. Each byte selects one 4 \u00d7 4 character tile through the split table at $08D6/$09C6."
  },
  {
   "address": 61568,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage 3 grid, 68 entries per row and first 9 rows. The engine uses the low three bits for world-coordinate attribute lookups and modifies the grid during play."
  },
  {
   "address": 62272,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage 4 grid, 20 entries per row and first 6 rows. Each byte selects one 4 \u00d7 4 character tile through the split table at $08D6/$09C6."
  },
  {
   "address": 62416,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage 4 grid, 20 entries per row and first 6 rows. The engine uses the low three bits for world-coordinate attribute lookups and modifies the grid during play."
  },
  {
   "address": 62594,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Saves the background latch, disables sprites and alternates its bit 3. When the flag at $F480 is set, also increments the extended background colours and advances indexed entries for up to 80 passes before restoring the latch."
  },
  {
   "address": 64704,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The one-based mission number used for this file and for play selection in the resident engine."
  },
  {
   "address": 64705,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Four split pointers with their high bytes at $FCC5. The resident loader at $0B26 selects a stage and gives its grid to the row-pointer builder at $0B46."
  },
  {
   "address": 64713,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Four split pointers with high bytes at $FCCD. The grid parallels the tile map and the resident coordinate lookup at $3DFA masks each attribute to its low three bits."
  },
  {
   "address": 64721,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage widths used as a byte stride for the tile and attribute row pointers."
  },
  {
   "address": 64725,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage heights used by the resident scaler to derive the vertical playfield limit and by $8EAD to walk the attribute grid."
  },
  {
   "address": 64729,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Indexed stage values copied to $2D during setup by $0AFD."
  },
  {
   "address": 64733,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "VIC extended background register $D022 values selected by stage."
  },
  {
   "address": 64737,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "VIC extended background register $D023 values selected by stage."
  },
  {
   "address": 64741,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Indexed initial view value written to $1781 before the character drawing loop at $1785."
  },
  {
   "address": 64745,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Four split pointers with high bytes at $FCED. $8FE8 copies 128 bytes from the selected source into a separate workspace half for each player."
  },
  {
   "address": 64753,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Indexed stage bytes cached at $0AEA and $0BE0 before display setup."
  },
  {
   "address": 64757,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage index compared at $1A82. A match enables the alternate source at $D800 and installs the two operand bytes following this value at $1642/$1643."
  },
  {
   "address": 64760,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Four indexed values. Stage setup at $0B0E copies the selected value to $1901."
  },
  {
   "address": 64764,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The pair at $FCFC/$FCFD supplies the two operand bytes at $2B0A/$2B0B."
  },
  {
   "address": 64766,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Low and high bytes of the mission-provided routine that $1AB3 calls after preparing the stage grids."
  },
  {
   "address": 64896,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage 1 placement seed copied into player workspace by $8FE8. A record has a destination low byte, destination high byte and value. A zero value ends the loop that applies records to the working stage grid."
  },
  {
   "address": 65024,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stage 2 placement seed copied into page $0200. The resident setup applies the value of each record at its two-byte destination and stops at the first zero value."
  },
  {
   "address": 65152,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Placement records shared by stages 3 and 4 in this mission, with an in-game destination word followed by a value byte. The loader supplies $70 bytes of this workspace source before the overlay ends at $FEEF."
  }
 ]
}